From e4180d75354006a0c6f9865b3535314b213961b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 22:15:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a /slug in a URL or path is not a board
 reference [daveey]

create_overlap refused seven unrelated creates on 2026-10-29 14:01-15:01 PDT
(hub t_01a189b2d186a986). Three changes:

1. A plain-word slug (hermes, bb, runners) is referenced only by `board <slug>`,
   `--board <slug>`, `<slug> board`, `@task:<slug>@gw/...` or `<gateway>/<slug>`
   as a whole token (hub/runners). `/<slug>` inside a URL, path or slash list
   (github.com/daveey/hermes, ~/code/hermes, Slack/Discord/BB Inbox) no longer
   counts. A non-plain slug keeps 004623277d's rules (/unconventional-collab
   anywhere, the slug in the title).
2. Naming a plain-word board needs 2 shared title words that are >= 25% of the
   longer title. One word ("skill", "create") or the hostname David-MBP matched
   some card on a board of hundreds by chance.
3. The hub replica's frozen legacy `<board>/<id>` row no longer outvotes its
   qualified `<profile>/<board>/<id>` twin: done t_d6973c6f was named via its
   legacy "running" row.

Problem: 7 creates refused (ci-flaky-cards x3, three chat cards, this card's
  own first create); every named card was unrelated, one done since 10-26.
Why 1: _names_board('hermes', ...) is True for any body with a daveey/hermes CI
  link: _explicit_board_ref matched `/` + slug anywhere.
Why 2: 004623277d kept `/slug` as "explicit" because it is the gateway/board
  form (hub/runners); the regex had no notion of which token precedes the `/`.
Why 3: the board rule needed only one shared title word, sized for the
  hyphenated Stage B case, so a weak signal on a plain-word board refused.
Why 4 (done card): the replica query filtered status per row before the
  dedupe, and the legacy pre-profile row (version 4, last written 10-2x) still
  says running.
Root (happened): board-reference detection was a substring rule with no model
  of URLs/paths, and the evidence bar did not scale with how common the slug
  and the shared words are.
Root (not caught): 004623277d's tests came from one incident (a bare word in a
  title) and asserted only bare-word negatives and `/slug` positives; no test
  put a plain-word slug inside a URL or path, though the core repo's own name
  is `hermes`. No test seeded a legacy replica row next to its qualified twin.
Recurrence: second fix to this guard in a day; the first fixed the reported
  shape only. This adds the observed corpus (real titles and trigger lines)
  as regression cases so the next shape is checked against all of them.

Tests: tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_url_slug.py (25, red on base),
  test_explicit_board_reference_still_names_the_board now shares >= 2 words
  and also asserts one shared word does not refuse.
